        "summary":  "Amazon Bedrock AgentCore enables autonomous business intelligence by orchestrating data across fragmented enterprise systems using MCP server connectors, policy enforcement, and isolated runtime environments. A manufacturing scenario demonstrates how different user personas receive personalized insights from disparate data sources without manual integration. The architecture separates agent orchestration, data access governance, and runtime isolation into distinct layers.",
        "execSummary":  "AWS is productizing autonomous business intelligence on Bedrock AgentCore, showing how MCP servers can connect siloed enterprise data into a governed, persona-aware insights pipeline ΓÇö a pattern directly relevant to operations and support leaders managing complex data landscapes. The key enterprise value is eliminating manual data consolidation by letting agents pull from multiple systems under policy controls, reducing time-to-insight for frontline and executive users alike. For customer-support leaders, this architecture suggests a credible path to agents that autonomously surface case context, customer history, and business signals without human-in-the-loop data gathering. The caveat: the MCP connector ecosystem is still maturing, and integrating proprietary or legacy systems will require significant engineering investment beyond what AWS demos typically show.",
