        "execSummary":  "The MCP protocol\u0027s shift to a stateless HTTP model is a significant infrastructure development for enterprise AI teams building multi-agent systems, because it means agent orchestration layers can now run on commodity web infrastructure rather than requiring persistent connection management. AWS\u0027s rapid AgentCore Gateway support for the new spec signals that the MCP ecosystem is stabilizing around open standards, which reduces lock-in risk for enterprises evaluating agent platforms. For technology leaders, this is the right moment to assess whether your agentic architecture is aligned with emerging MCP standards, since early standardization decisions tend to compound. The caveat is that the spec is brand-new and real-world implementation edge cases across complex enterprise toolchains will take months to surface.",
