        "theme":  "Support",
        "summary":  "The article demonstrates building an automated customer retention pipeline using Amazon Quick components ΓÇö Dashboard, Chat Agent, Flows, and Automate ΓÇö to identify at-risk customers from contact center data and call transcripts. The solution combines structured KPI analysis with AI-powered sentiment analysis and custom scoring logic via MCP Actions to generate personalized retention offers. Response time for at-risk customer identification drops from days to minutes.",
        "execSummary":  "AWS is showcasing a production-ready pattern for AI-driven customer retention that directly applies to contact center and CX operations: ingest call transcript data, apply sentiment and churn-risk scoring, and trigger personalized intervention offers ΓÇö all without human routing. For customer-support leaders, the days-to-minutes response-time reduction is the headline number, but the deeper implication is that this architecture enables proactive retention at a scale impossible with traditional case-by-case review. The MCP Actions integration also means the same framework can plug into broader agent ecosystems, making retention logic a reusable module rather than a siloed tool. Watch for data quality and model calibration challenges: AI churn scores are only as good as the training signals, and false positives in high-value customer segments carry real business cost.",
