        "execSummary":  "CIOs face compounding pressure as AI accelerates the pace of strategic decision-making, turning previously manageable trade-offs into high-stakes choices that can define enterprise competitiveness. The article identifies six recurring tension points ΓÇö including build vs. buy, stability vs. innovation, and cost vs. capability ΓÇö that now demand explicit governance rather than ad-hoc resolution. For enterprise leaders, the key implication is that AI does not eliminate these trade-offs; it raises the cost of getting them wrong. Organizations without a documented decision framework for these tensions risk inconsistent execution and misaligned investment.",
